# This host's own osquery flags: the server it talks to and how it enrolls.
# vajra_install.sh writes it (and pins the host identifier below); agent
# updates never change it.
#
# The flags every host shares are in vajra.flags, which agent updates ship.
# It must stay the first flag: whichever line sets a flag last wins, so the
# lines after it decide the server and identity even if vajra.flags names
# them too. osqueryd won't start if vajra.flags is missing.
--flagfile=/etc/osquery/vajra.flags
--tls_hostname=YOUR_SERVER_HOST:1234
--host_identifier=uuid
